🌐 STEP 0: Open AWS Console
Go to 👉 https://aws.amazon.com/console
Click “Sign in to Console”
Login

At the top, you’ll see a search bar (very important — we’ll use this everywhere)

🪣 STEP 1: Create S3 Bucket
🔍 Find S3
In top search bar → type S3
Click S3 (Simple Storage Service)
➕ Create Bucket
On S3 page → click “Create bucket” (big orange button)
📝 Fill details
Bucket name → type: my-first-bucket-harsha (must be unique)
Region → leave default
⚙️ Scroll down
Find “Bucket Versioning”
Click Enable
✅ Create
Scroll down → click “Create bucket”

✔️ Done

🗄️ STEP 2: Create DynamoDB Table
🔍 Open DynamoDB
Search → DynamoDB
Click it
➕ Create Table
Click “Create table”
📝 Fill details
Table name → newtable
Partition key:
Name → unique
Type → String

👉 Leave everything else default

✅ Create
Click “Create table”

✔️ Done

⚡ STEP 3: Create Lambda Function
🔍 Open Lambda
Search → Lambda
Click it
➕ Create Function
Click “Create function”
🧱 Choose
Select → Author from scratch
📝 Fill details
Function name → S3ToDynamoFunction
Runtime → choose Python 3.x
🔐 Permissions
Select:
Create a new role with basic Lambda permissions
✅ Create
Click “Create function”

✔️ Done

🔗 STEP 4: Add S3 Trigger

Inside your Lambda page:

➕ Add Trigger
Click “Add trigger” (left side)
⚙️ Configure
Trigger type → select S3
Bucket → choose your bucket (my-first-bucket-harsha)
Event type → select:
All object create events
☑️ Checkbox
Tick: “I acknowledge…”
✅ Add
Click “Add”

✔️ Done

💻 STEP 5: Add Code
🧾 Find Code Editor
Scroll down in Lambda page
You’ll see Code Source editor
✏️ Replace existing code with this:
import boto3
from uuid import uuid4

def lambda_handler(event, context):
    dynamodb = boto3.resource('dynamodb')

    if 'Records' in event:
        for record in event['Records']:
            bucket_name = record['s3']['bucket']['name']
            object_key = record['s3']['object']['key']
            size = record['s3']['object'].get('size', -1)
            event_name = record.get('eventName', 'Unknown')
            event_time = record.get('eventTime', 'Unknown')

            table = dynamodb.Table('newtable')

            table.put_item(
                Item={
                    'unique': str(uuid4()),
                    'Bucket': bucket_name,
                    'Object': object_key,
                    'Size': size,
                    'Event': event_name,
                    'EventTime': event_time
                }
            )
    else:
        print("No Records found")
⚠️ IMPORTANT
If your table name ≠ newtable, change it
If partition key ≠ unique, change it
💾 Save & Deploy
Click “Deploy” (orange button)

✔️ Done

🔐 STEP 5.5 (ONLY if error comes)

If you get permission error, do this:

🔍 Open IAM
Search → IAM
Click
👤 Roles
Click Roles
Click your Lambda role (name will be similar)
➕ Add Permission
Click Add permissions
Click Create inline policy
🧾 JSON tab

Paste:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "dynamodb:PutItem",
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}
✅ Create
Click Next
Name → lambda-dynamo-policy
Click Create policy

✔️ Done

